# PIXELTRUTH Software Architecture

## 1. Status and scope

This is the initial architecture specification derived from the PIXELTRUTH master prompt. The current workspace had no application source, Git metadata, or existing architecture file at the time this document was created. The module layout below is therefore the proposed baseline; inspect the actual project before implementing it. Do not migrate or restructure existing code without review and approval.

## 2. Architectural goals

- Keep image analysis independent of Streamlit wherever practical.
- Keep processing local and in memory by default.
- Separate file validation, properties, metadata, integrity rules, assessment, comparison, analysis, reporting, and presentation.
- Make each finding explainable and traceable to observed evidence.
- Keep optional or unsupported analyses explicit.
- Use shared typed data structures and avoid duplicate parsing or formatting logic.

